/-!
# Full sets of sections

Let `B` be a commutative `A`-algebra, finite and locally free as an `A`-module, so that
`Z = Spec B → Spec A` is finite locally free. An `A`-algebra map `B →ₐ[A] A` is a section of
`Z`. A family of sections `s : ι → (B →ₐ[A] A)` is a *full set of sections* (Katz–Mazur §1.8)
when, after every base change `A → T`, the norm of every function on `Z_T` is the product of its
values at the sections:

  `Norm_{T ⊗[A] B / T} (f) = ∏ i, sᵢ(f)`  for all `f ∈ T ⊗[A] B`.

The quantification over base changes is part of the definition. Full sets of sections are how
Katz and Mazur express, over an arbitrary base, that a finite flat scheme "consists of" given
points counted with multiplicity: Drinfeld level structures on elliptic curves are defined by
asking that the points of a homomorphism `(ℤ/N)² → E[N]`, or the multiples of a point, form a
full set of sections of a finite locally free subgroup scheme.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.IsFullSetOfSections s`: the family `s` is a full set of sections of `B` over `A`.
  The norm is tested on the base changes `T ⊗[A] B` which are free over `T`; when `B` is free over
  `A` this is every base change, and every finite projective `B` is free Zariski-locally on
  `Spec A`.
* `TauCeti.fullSetPolynomial b u`: for a family `u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C` into an `A`-algebra `C`, the
  generic norm form of `B` in the basis `b` minus the product of the linear forms
  `∑ j, uᵢ(bⱼ) • Xⱼ`.
* `TauCeti.fullSetIdeal u`: the ideal of `C` generated by the coefficients of that polynomial; it
  cuts out the full-set locus `Spec (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u)` of `Spec C`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isFullSetOfSections_comp_algEquiv_iff`: being a full set of sections is invariant under
  isomorphisms of `B`.

In the remaining results, `B` is free of finite rank over `A`.

* `TauCeti.IsFullSetOfSections.norm_eq`: the defining identity holds for test algebras in every
  universe.
* `TauCeti.isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod`: the reduction to the universal case
  (Katz–Mazur, proof of 1.9.1). For a basis `b` of `B` indexed by `κ`, `s` is a full set of
  sections if and only if the norm form factors into linear forms,
  `Norm (∑ j, Xⱼ ⊗ bⱼ) = ∏ i, ∑ j, sᵢ(bⱼ) • Xⱼ` in `MvPolynomial κ A`.
* `TauCeti.isFullSetOfSections_iff_charpoly`: the characteristic-polynomial formulation
  (Katz–Mazur 1.8.2).
* `TauCeti.IsFullSetOfSections.baseChange`, `TauCeti.IsFullSetOfSections.of_baseChange` and
  `TauCeti.isFullSetOfSections_baseChange_iff`: full sets of sections are stable under arbitrary
  base change and descend along injective ring maps, in particular along faithfully flat ones.
* `TauCeti.IsFullSetOfSections.card_eq_finrank`: over a nontrivial ring, a full set of sections
  has exactly `rank B` members.
* `TauCeti.isFullSetOfSections_evalAlgHom`: the coordinate projections of `ι → A`, the sections
  of the constant scheme `⨆_{i ∈ ι} Spec A`, form a full set of sections.
* `TauCeti.IsFullSetOfSections.prod`: full sets of sections of `B₁` and `B₂` together form one of
  `B₁ × B₂` (Katz–Mazur 1.8.4).
* `TauCeti.isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff`: the full-set locus (Katz–Mazur 1.9.1, over
  an affine base and for `B` free). For `φ : C →ₐ[A] T`, the family `φ ∘ u` is a full set of
  sections of `T ⊗[A] B` over `T` if and only if `φ` kills `fullSetIdeal u`.
  `TauCeti.quotientFullSetIdealHomEquiv` is the resulting universal property of
  `C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u`.
* `TauCeti.fullSetIdeal_eq_span`, `TauCeti.fullSetIdeal_fg` and `TauCeti.map_fullSetIdeal`: the
  full-set ideal does not depend on the basis, is finitely generated, and commutes with base
  change of the ambient algebra `C`.

## References

* N. M. Katz, B. Mazur, *Arithmetic Moduli of Elliptic Curves*, Annals of Mathematics Studies
  108, Princeton University Press, 1985, §§1.8–1.9.
-/

public section

open TensorProduct MvPolynomial

namespace TauCeti

universe u v w

variable {A : Type u} {B : Type v} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
variable {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]

/-- A family `s` of `A`-algebra maps `B →ₐ[A] A`, that is, of sections of `Spec B → Spec A`, is a
*full set of sections* (Katz–Mazur §1.8) if after every base change `A → T` the norm of every
`f ∈ T ⊗[A] B` over `T` is the product `∏ i, sᵢ(f)` of the values of `f` at the base-changed
sections. Norms are taken on the base changes `T ⊗[A] B` which are free over `T`, where
`Algebra.norm` is the determinant of multiplication. -/
def IsFullSetOfSections (s : ι → B →ₐ[A] A) : Prop :=
  ∀ (T : Type u) [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] [Module.Free T (T ⊗[A] B)] (f : T ⊗[A] B),
    Algebra.norm T f = ∏ i, (s i).sectionBaseChange T f

variable {s : ι → B →ₐ[A] A}

/-- Unfolding `IsFullSetOfSections`: the norm identity holds on every base change `T ⊗[A] B` which
is free over `T`, for `T` in the universe of `A`. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_iff : IsFullSetOfSections s ↔
    ∀ (T : Type u) [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] [Module.Free T (T ⊗[A] B)] (f : T ⊗[A] B),
      Algebra.norm T f = ∏ i, (s i).sectionBaseChange T f :=
  Iff.rfl

-- The base change of `e : B ≃ₐ[A] B'` identifies the norms and the values at the sections.
private theorem IsFullSetOfSections.of_comp_algEquiv {B' : Type*} [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B']
    (e : B ≃ₐ[A] B') {s : ι → B' →ₐ[A] A}
    (h : IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ (s i).comp e.toAlgHom) : IsFullSetOfSections s := by
  intro T _ _ _ f
  let eT := Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl : T ≃ₐ[T] T) e
  have : Module.Free T (T ⊗[A] B) := .of_equiv eT.symm.toLinearEquiv
  rw [← Algebra.norm_eq_of_algEquiv eT.symm, h T]
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  induction f using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul x y => simp [eT]
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]

/-- Being a full set of sections is invariant under isomorphism: for `e : B ≃ₐ[A] B'` and sections
`s` of `B'`, the sections `sᵢ ∘ e` of `B` form a full set if and only if the `sᵢ` do. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_comp_algEquiv_iff {B' : Type*} [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B']
    (e : B ≃ₐ[A] B') {s : ι → B' →ₐ[A] A} :
    (IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ (s i).comp e.toAlgHom) ↔ IsFullSetOfSections s :=
  ⟨.of_comp_algEquiv e, fun h ↦ .of_comp_algEquiv e.symm (by simpa [AlgHom.comp_assoc] using h)⟩

section Free

variable [Module.Free A B] [Module.Finite A B]

/-- If the norm form of `B` in a basis `b` factors as `∏ i, ∑ j, sᵢ(bⱼ) • Xⱼ`, then the norm on
every base change `T ⊗[A] B` is the product of the values at the sections: write
`f = ∑ j, cⱼ ⊗ bⱼ` and specialize `Xⱼ ↦ cⱼ`. -/
private theorem norm_eq_prod_of_generic {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : Module.Basis κ A B)
    (h : Algebra.norm (MvPolynomial κ A) (∑ j, (X j : MvPolynomial κ A) ⊗ₜ[A] b j) =
      ∏ i, ∑ j, s i (b j) • (X j : MvPolynomial κ A))
    (T : Type w) [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] (f : T ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.norm T f = ∏ i, (s i).sectionBaseChange T f := by
  classical
  set c := (Algebra.TensorProduct.basis T b).repr f
  have hf : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (aeval (fun j ↦ c j))
      (∑ j, (X j : MvPolynomial κ A) ⊗ₜ[A] b j) = f := by
    conv_rhs => rw [← (Algebra.TensorProduct.basis T b).sum_repr f]
    simp [c, TensorProduct.smul_tmul']
  rw [← hf, Algebra.norm_rTensor, h, map_prod]
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [AlgHom.sectionBaseChange_rTensor, AlgHom.sectionBaseChange_sum_tmul]

/-- The defining identity of a full set of sections holds after base change to a commutative
`A`-algebra `T` in any universe. -/
theorem IsFullSetOfSections.norm_eq (h : IsFullSetOfSections s) (T : Type w) [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] (f : T ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.norm T f = ∏ i, (s i).sectionBaseChange T f :=
  norm_eq_prod_of_generic ((Module.Free.chooseBasis A B).reindex (Fintype.equivFin _))
    ((h _ _).trans (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun _ _ ↦ AlgHom.sectionBaseChange_sum_tmul _ _ _ _)) T f

/-- **Reduction to the universal case** (Katz–Mazur, proof of 1.9.1). For a basis `b` of `B`
indexed by `κ`, a family of sections `s` is a full set of sections if and only if the norm of the
generic element `∑ j, Xⱼ ⊗ bⱼ` of `MvPolynomial κ A ⊗[A] B` is the product of the linear forms
`∑ j, sᵢ(bⱼ) • Xⱼ`. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : Module.Basis κ A B) :
    IsFullSetOfSections s ↔
      Algebra.norm (MvPolynomial κ A) (∑ j, (X j : MvPolynomial κ A) ⊗ₜ[A] b j) =
        ∏ i, ∑ j, s i (b j) • (X j : MvPolynomial κ A) :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ (h.norm_eq _ _).trans
      (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun _ _ ↦ AlgHom.sectionBaseChange_sum_tmul _ _ _ _),
    fun h T _ _ _ f ↦ norm_eq_prod_of_generic b h T f⟩

/-- A full set of sections remains one after an arbitrary base change `A → T`. -/
theorem IsFullSetOfSections.baseChange (h : IsFullSetOfSections s) (T : Type w) [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] : IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ (s i).sectionBaseChange T := by
  let b := Module.Free.chooseBasis A B
  rw [isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod (Algebra.TensorProduct.basis T b),
    Algebra.norm_sum_X_tmul_tensorProductBasis, (isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod b).1 h]
  simp [map_prod, Algebra.smul_def]

/-- Being a full set of sections descends along an injective ring map `A → T`, in particular
along a faithfully flat one. -/
theorem IsFullSetOfSections.of_baseChange {T : Type w} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T]
    (hT : Function.Injective (algebraMap A T))
    (h : IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ (s i).sectionBaseChange T) : IsFullSetOfSections s := by
  let b := Module.Free.chooseBasis A B
  rw [isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod b]
  apply MvPolynomial.map_injective _ hT
  have := (isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod (Algebra.TensorProduct.basis T b)).1 h
  rw [Algebra.norm_sum_X_tmul_tensorProductBasis] at this
  simpa [map_prod, Algebra.smul_def] using this

/-- Over a base change which is injective, being a full set of sections can be checked after the
base change. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_baseChange_iff {T : Type w} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T]
    (hT : Function.Injective (algebraMap A T)) :
    (IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ (s i).sectionBaseChange T) ↔ IsFullSetOfSections s :=
  ⟨.of_baseChange hT, fun h ↦ h.baseChange T⟩

/-- Over a nontrivial ring, a full set of sections has as many members as the rank of `B`. -/
theorem IsFullSetOfSections.card_eq_finrank [Nontrivial A] (h : IsFullSetOfSections s) :
    Fintype.card ι = Module.finrank A B := by
  have := h.norm_eq (Polynomial A) (algebraMap (Polynomial A) _ Polynomial.X)
  rw [Algebra.norm_algebraMap, Module.finrank_baseChange] at this
  simpa using congrArg Polynomial.natDegree this.symm

/-- The characteristic polynomial of multiplication by `f` on a base change of `B` by a full set
of sections is `∏ i, (X - sᵢ(f))`, for test algebras in any universe. -/
theorem IsFullSetOfSections.charpoly_eq (h : IsFullSetOfSections s) (T : Type w) [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] (f : T ⊗[A] B) :
    (Algebra.lmul T (T ⊗[A] B) f).charpoly =
      ∏ i, (Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C ((s i).sectionBaseChange T f)) := by
  rw [Algebra.charpoly_lmul_eq_norm, h.norm_eq]
  simp [Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]

/-- **Characteristic-polynomial formulation** (Katz–Mazur 1.8.2). A family of sections `s` is a
full set of sections if and only if after every base change `A → T` the characteristic polynomial
of multiplication by every `f ∈ T ⊗[A] B` is `∏ i, (X - sᵢ(f))`. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_iff_charpoly :
    IsFullSetOfSections s ↔ ∀ (T : Type u) [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] (f : T ⊗[A] B),
      (Algebra.lmul T (T ⊗[A] B) f).charpoly =
        ∏ i, (Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C ((s i).sectionBaseChange T f)) := by
  refine ⟨fun h T _ _ f ↦ h.charpoly_eq T f, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  intro T _ _ _ f
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial T with _ | _
  · exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  have hdeg := congrArg Polynomial.natDegree (h T f)
  rw [LinearMap.charpoly_natDegree, Polynomial.natDegree_finsetProd_X_sub_C_eq_card,
    Finset.card_univ] at hdeg
  rw [Algebra.norm_apply, LinearMap.det_eq_sign_charpoly_coeff, h T f,
    Polynomial.coeff_zero_eq_eval_zero, Polynomial.eval_prod, hdeg]
  simp [Finset.prod_neg, ← mul_assoc, ← pow_add]

end Free

/-- The coordinate projections `ι → A`, the sections of the constant finite scheme
`⨆_{i ∈ ι} Spec A`, form a full set of sections. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_evalAlgHom :
    IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ Pi.evalAlgHom A (fun _ : ι ↦ A) i := by
  classical
  intro T _ _ _ f
  rw [← Algebra.norm_eq_of_algEquiv (Algebra.TensorProduct.piScalarRight A T T ι),
    Algebra.norm_pi]
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [Algebra.norm_self, MonoidHom.id_apply]
  induction f using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul t y => simp [Algebra.smul_def, mul_comm]
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, Pi.add_apply, hx, hy]

/-- **Disjoint unions** (Katz–Mazur 1.8.4). If `s₁` and `s₂` are full sets of sections of `B₁`
and `B₂`, then their composites with the two projections together form a full set of sections of
`B₁ × B₂`. -/
theorem IsFullSetOfSections.prod {B₁ B₂ : Type*} [CommRing B₁] [Algebra A B₁] [CommRing B₂]
    [Algebra A B₂] [Module.Free A B₁] [Module.Finite A B₁] [Module.Free A B₂]
    [Module.Finite A B₂] {ι₁ ι₂ : Type*} [Fintype ι₁] [Fintype ι₂] {s₁ : ι₁ → B₁ →ₐ[A] A}
    {s₂ : ι₂ → B₂ →ₐ[A] A} (h₁ : IsFullSetOfSections s₁) (h₂ : IsFullSetOfSections s₂) :
    IsFullSetOfSections (Sum.elim (fun i ↦ (s₁ i).comp (AlgHom.fst A B₁ B₂))
      fun i ↦ (s₂ i).comp (AlgHom.snd A B₁ B₂)) := by
  intro T _ _ _ f
  rw [← Algebra.norm_eq_of_algEquiv (Algebra.TensorProduct.prodRight A T T B₁ B₂),
    Algebra.norm_prod, h₁.norm_eq, h₂.norm_eq, Fintype.prod_sum_type]
  congr 1 <;> refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_ <;>
  induction f using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul t y => simp
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, Prod.fst_add, Prod.snd_add, hx, hy]

/-! ### The full-set locus

A family of `A`-algebra maps `u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C` into an `A`-algebra `C` is a family of sections
of `Spec (C ⊗[A] B) → Spec C`, for instance the universal family on a scheme of tuples of sections
or of homomorphisms of finite group schemes. The points of `Spec C` over which it is a full set of
sections form a closed subscheme `Spec (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u)`, cut out by the coefficients of the
norm identity in a basis of `B`. -/

section Locus

variable {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]

/-- The *norm-identity polynomial* of a family `u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C` in a basis `b` of `B`: the
generic norm form `Norm (∑ j, Xⱼ ⊗ bⱼ)` of `B` minus the product of the linear forms
`∑ j, uᵢ(bⱼ) • Xⱼ`, in `MvPolynomial κ C`. Its coefficients are equations for the locus over
which `u` is a full set of sections. -/
noncomputable def fullSetPolynomial {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : Module.Basis κ A B)
    (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) : MvPolynomial κ C :=
  MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A C)
      (Algebra.norm (MvPolynomial κ A) (∑ j, (X j : MvPolynomial κ A) ⊗ₜ[A] b j)) -
    ∏ i, ∑ j, u i (b j) • (X j : MvPolynomial κ C)

/-- The norm-identity polynomial is natural in the ambient algebra `C`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_fullSetPolynomial {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : Module.Basis κ A B)
    (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) {C' : Type*} [CommRing C'] [Algebra A C'] (ψ : C →ₐ[A] C') :
    MvPolynomial.map ψ (fullSetPolynomial b u) = fullSetPolynomial b fun i ↦ ψ.comp (u i) := by
  simp [fullSetPolynomial, map_prod, MvPolynomial.map_map, Algebra.smul_def]

variable [Module.Free A B] [Module.Finite A B]

/-- **The full-set equations.** A family `u : ι → B →ₐ[A] T` gives sections of
`T ⊗[A] B` over `T`, and these form a full set of sections exactly when the norm-identity
polynomial of `u` in a basis of `B` vanishes. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_iff {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : Module.Basis κ A B)
    {T : Type w} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] T) :
    IsFullSetOfSections (fun i ↦ AlgHom.liftEquiv A T B T (u i)) ↔
      fullSetPolynomial b u = 0 := by
  rw [isFullSetOfSections_iff_norm_eq_prod (Algebra.TensorProduct.basis T b),
    Algebra.norm_sum_X_tmul_tensorProductBasis, fullSetPolynomial, sub_eq_zero]
  simp

/-- The ideal of the *full-set locus* of a family `u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C`: it is generated by the
coefficients of the norm-identity polynomial of `u` in a basis of `B`, and the closed subscheme
`Spec (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u)` of `Spec C` is the locus over which `u` is a full set of sections
(`isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff`). It does not depend on the basis
(`fullSetIdeal_eq_span`). -/
noncomputable def fullSetIdeal (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) : Ideal C :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun m ↦ (fullSetPolynomial (Module.Free.chooseBasis A B) u).coeff m)

/-- The ideal generated by the coefficients of the norm-identity polynomial in a basis `b` lies in
the kernel of `φ` if and only if `φ ∘ u` is a full set of sections. -/
private theorem span_coeff_fullSetPolynomial_le_ker_iff {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ]
    (b : Module.Basis κ A B) (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) {T : Type w} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T]
    (φ : C →ₐ[A] T) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range fun m ↦ (fullSetPolynomial b u).coeff m) ≤ RingHom.ker φ ↔
      IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ AlgHom.liftEquiv A T B T (φ.comp (u i)) := by
  rw [isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_iff b, ← map_fullSetPolynomial, ← RingHom.mem_ker,
    MvPolynomial.ker_map, MvPolynomial.mem_map_C_iff, Ideal.span_le, Set.range_subset_iff]
  simp

/-- **The full-set locus** (Katz–Mazur 1.9.1). For an `A`-algebra map `φ : C →ₐ[A] T`, the
family `φ ∘ u` is a full set of sections of `T ⊗[A] B` over `T` if and only if `φ` kills
`fullSetIdeal u`, that is, `Spec T → Spec C` factors through `Spec (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u)`. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) {T : Type w} [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] (φ : C →ₐ[A] T) :
    IsFullSetOfSections (fun i ↦ AlgHom.liftEquiv A T B T (φ.comp (u i))) ↔
      fullSetIdeal u ≤ RingHom.ker φ :=
  (span_coeff_fullSetPolynomial_le_ker_iff _ u φ).symm

/-- The full-set ideal is generated by the coefficients of the norm-identity polynomial in any
basis of `B`: the full-set locus does not depend on the choice of basis. -/
theorem fullSetIdeal_eq_span {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : Module.Basis κ A B)
    (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) :
    fullSetIdeal u = Ideal.span (Set.range fun m ↦ (fullSetPolynomial b u).coeff m) := by
  have hker (I : Ideal C) : RingHom.ker (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A I) = I := by
    rw [AlgHom.ker_coe, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_ker]
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [← hker (Ideal.span _), ← isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff,
      ← span_coeff_fullSetPolynomial_le_ker_iff b, hker]
  · rw [← hker (fullSetIdeal u), span_coeff_fullSetPolynomial_le_ker_iff b,
      isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff, hker]

/-- The full-set ideal is finitely generated, so the full-set locus is a closed subscheme of finite
presentation. -/
theorem fullSetIdeal_fg (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) : (fullSetIdeal u).FG := by
  rw [fullSetIdeal]
  generalize fullSetPolynomial (Module.Free.chooseBasis A B) u = p
  refine ⟨p.coeffs, le_antisymm (Ideal.span_mono fun c hc ↦ ?_) (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_)⟩
  · obtain ⟨m, -, rfl⟩ := MvPolynomial.mem_coeffs_iff.1 hc
    exact ⟨m, rfl⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
    by_cases hm : p.coeff m = 0
    · simp [hm]
    · exact Ideal.subset_span (MvPolynomial.coeff_mem_coeffs m hm)

/-- **Base change of the full-set locus** in the ambient algebra: along `ψ : C →ₐ[A] C'`, the
full-set ideal of `ψ ∘ u` is generated by the image of that of `u`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_fullSetIdeal (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) {C' : Type*} [CommRing C'] [Algebra A C']
    (ψ : C →ₐ[A] C') : (fullSetIdeal u).map ψ = fullSetIdeal fun i ↦ ψ.comp (u i) := by
  rw [fullSetIdeal, fullSetIdeal, ← map_fullSetPolynomial _ u ψ, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  simp only [Function.comp_def, MvPolynomial.coeff_map, RingHom.coe_coe]

/-- The family `u` becomes a full set of sections on the full-set locus `C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u`. -/
theorem isFullSetOfSections_quotient_fullSetIdeal (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) :
    IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ AlgHom.liftEquiv A (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u) B (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u)
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A (fullSetIdeal u)).comp (u i)) :=
  (isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff u _).2 (by rw [AlgHom.ker_coe, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_ker])

/-- **Universal property of the full-set locus.** `A`-algebra maps out of `C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u`
correspond to the `A`-algebra maps `φ : C →ₐ[A] T` along which `u` becomes a full set of
sections: `Spec (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u)` represents the subfunctor of `Spec C` over which `u` is a
full set of sections. -/
noncomputable def quotientFullSetIdealHomEquiv (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) (T : Type w) [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] :
    (C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u →ₐ[A] T) ≃
      {φ : C →ₐ[A] T // IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ AlgHom.liftEquiv A T B T (φ.comp (u i))} where
  toFun g := ⟨g.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A _), (isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff u _).2
    fun x hx ↦ by simp [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 hx]⟩
  invFun φ := Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ φ fun _ hx ↦ (isFullSetOfSections_liftEquiv_comp_iff u _).1
    φ.2 hx
  left_inv g := Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext A (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ_comp _ _ _)
  right_inv φ := Subtype.ext (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ_comp _ _ _)

/-- The map `C →ₐ[A] T` attached to `g : C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u →ₐ[A] T` is `g` composed with the
quotient map. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_quotientFullSetIdealHomEquiv_apply (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) {T : Type w} [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] (g : C ⧸ fullSetIdeal u →ₐ[A] T) :
    (quotientFullSetIdealHomEquiv u T g : C →ₐ[A] T) = g.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A _) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The map out of the full-set locus attached to `φ` is the map induced by `φ` on the quotient. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientFullSetIdealHomEquiv_symm_apply_mk (u : ι → B →ₐ[A] C) {T : Type w}
    [CommRing T] [Algebra A T]
    (φ : {φ : C →ₐ[A] T // IsFullSetOfSections fun i ↦ AlgHom.liftEquiv A T B T (φ.comp (u i))})
    (x : C) : (quotientFullSetIdealHomEquiv u T).symm φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) = φ.1 x :=
  (rfl)

end Locus

end TauCeti
